From bae9d565c7d6ec662893832b4a016813434ab8e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:04:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] uhf: complete the sect4.9 buffered inventory public API
 (FR-BUF-01..04)

Closes a real gap from the Phase 1 commit: UhfSessionArbiter already had
startBufferedInventory/stopBufferedInventory (needed internally for the
FR-STR-13 stream-suspend bookkeeping), but nothing above it - not the
AIDL, not UhfSession, not UhfService - ever exposed buffered inventory to
a caller. An app had no way to reach a feature the arbiter was already
half-built to support.

Adds, end to end (AIDL -> UhfSession -> UhfService -> UhfSessionArbiter):
- startBufferedInventory(InventoryParams) - now takes Q/session, sent in
  the 0x18 payload (previously hardcoded to an empty payload).
- getBufferedTagCount() (0x19) and readBuffer() (0x72, reusing the same
  multi-frame assembly and status handling inventory() already uses -
  FR-BUF-03 says explicitly to handle it "as in FR-INV-02", so this reuses
  that path instead of writing a second copy of it).
- clearBuffer() - FR-BUF-04s explicit mid-session half, distinct from
  stopBufferedInventory()s automatic on-session-end half (both send the
  same 0x1A; the difference is only whether the buffered session ends).
- stopBufferedInventory() on the public API - not shown in the SRS's own
  sect4.9 code sample, but added anyway: without it there is no
  caller-reachable way to end buffered mode and get an interrupted stream
  back (FR-STR-13s restart half is otherwise unreachable).

All four are UHF_READ-gated (sect2.3 groups buffered inventory with polled/
streaming inventory as ordinary tag acquisition, not OEM configuration)
and all route through the same FR-STR-13 stop/apply/restart discipline
tag memory ops already use.

8 new arbiter tests (Q/session payload, count decode incl. a too-short-
reply rejection, buffer read success/empty/error paths reusing the tested
decoder, explicit-clear vs automatic-clear-on-stop). 100/100 total passing.

Cross-checked by script again: AIDL (37 methods) <-> BinderService <->
UhfManager/UhfSession <-> UhfSessionArbiter all match 1:1, no mismatches
this round.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
